specan_ui — graphical real-time spectrum analyzer for the Ubertooth.

Requirements:
  * Python 3.8+ (3.12+ also needs setuptools installed to build — PEP 632)
  * Python packages: numpy, qtpy, and a Qt binding (PySide6 or PyQt5)
  * The built Ubertooth host tools (provides ubertooth-specan)

Install (installs the launcher AND the specan Python package):
  $ cd host/build && cmake .. && make && sudo make install

Run:
  $ ubertooth-specan-ui          # or: sudo ubertooth-specan-ui  (device access)

Getting "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'specan'"? The specan package
was not installed for the Python running the launcher — usually because you
ran it without `make install`, or the build used a different Python than the
launcher. See the full install/run and troubleshooting guide:

  docs/source/specan_ui.rst
  (https://ubertooth.readthedocs.io/en/latest/specan_ui.html)
